{"id": "DeuK3ggxQsS", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Did you know YAMRAJ, the god of death himself, once DIED? 💀🔱 The story of Markandeya, the boy Death couldn't take.\n\nA sage begged Lord Shiva for a son. Shiva gave him a choice: a dull son who lives long, or a wise son who dies at 16. He chose the wise one: Markandeya.\n\nOn the day he was to die, the boy was praying to Shiva. Yama's messengers came, but could not even touch him. So Yamraj came himself, on his buffalo, and threw his noose. It fell round the boy… and round the Shiva linga he was hugging.\n\nShiva burst out of the linga and kicked Death in the chest. Yamraj fell, dead. And then nobody on Earth could die, until the Earth could bear it no more. Vishnu and the gods begged Shiva, and he brought Yama back, on one condition: Markandeya stays 16 forever.\n\nThat is why Shiva is called Kalantaka, the End of Death, and Mrityunjaya, the one who conquered it. The temple at Thirukkadaiyur in Tamil Nadu still tells this story.\n\n📚 15K FAMILY DEAL: our books 1–3 (Shailputri, Brahmacharini, Chandraghanta), illustrated mythology for kids, the set of 3 for just ₹350 (was ₹500). Extended till 25 Oct, midnight! Comment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio: rishikatha.com\n\n🔱 Save this, share it with someone who loves Mahadev, and comment HAR HAR MAHADEV!\n\n#Shiva #Mahadev #Yamraj #Markandeya #HarHarMahadev #Mahakal #Kalantaka #Mrityunjaya #HinduMythology #ShivaPurana #SanatanDharma #IndianMythology #Thirukkadaiyur #RishiKatha #MythologyForKids", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792510723, "like_count": 11396, "comment_count": 105, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1579770836806782a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 70.65, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.f